### 1. Login as Bob (saves token)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@hotel.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 2. Report an incident (saves incidentId)
POST http://localhost:8080/incidents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "type": "FIRE",
  "severity": "HIGH",
  "description": "Smoke reported in kitchen"
}

> {% client.global.set("incidentId", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Update status -> ACKNOWLEDGED  (expect version: 1)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/incidents/{{incidentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "ACKNOWLEDGED"
}

### 4. Update status -> IN_PROGRESS  (expect version: 2)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/incidents/{{incidentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

### 5. Get the event log  (expect CREATED + 2x STATUS_CHANGED)
GET http://localhost:8080/incidents/{{incidentId}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. List incidents (Bob's venue)
GET http://localhost:8080/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Tenancy checks (Carol, venue-2) ---

### 7. Register Carol (skip / 409 if she already exists)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carol@hotel2.com",
  "password": "pass123",
  "displayName": "Carol",
  "role": "STAFF",
  "venueId": "venue-2"
}

### 8. Login as Carol (overwrites token with Carol's)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carol@hotel2.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 9. Carol lists incidents -> expect []  (can't see venue-1)
GET http://localhost:8080/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Carol tries to update Bob's incident -> expect 403
PATCH http://localhost:8080/incidents/{{incidentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}
### Register with invalid data -> expect 400 with field errors
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123",
  "displayName": "",
  "role": "STAFF",
  "venueId": "venue-1"
}